  {
   "id": "1afZHoYaBQAJ",
   "from": "Mike Collyer",
   "author": "aab55242ff4da6c6",
   "date": "2017-10-18T15:56:36Z",
   "subject": "Re: [geomorph-r-package] Strange error using coords.subset",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Pedro,<div><br></div><div>The issue is that in your ind grouping you have some groups of size one and this function calls the arrayspecs function, which seems to have trouble wrangling with a vector of values rather than a matrix of values.  (This is an issue in R quite often; a single-column  or single-row matrix gets converted to a vector.  Sometimes one has to have a step to force it back into a matrix.)</div><div><br></div><div>When I get a chance, I’ll try to add a check into the function for such things.  We do not expect one would try to sort 24 values into 22 groups, so things like this elude us a bit.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers!</div><div>Mike</div><div><br><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
