   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Mike,<div><br></div><div>It wasn&#39;t supposed to have groups of size one. It was a typing error in one of the files I used to produce the groups. </div><div>As soon as I fixed the typing, the error disappeared. </div><div><br></div><div>Thank you!</div><div><br></div><div>Pedro</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">2017-10-18 13:56 GMT-02:00 Mike Collyer <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mlco...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span>:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Pedro,<div><br></div><div>The issue is that in your ind grouping you have some groups of size one and this function calls the arrayspecs function, which seems to have trouble wrangling with a vector of values rather than a matrix of values.  (This is an issue in R quite often; a single-column  or single-row matrix gets converted to a vector.  Sometimes one has to have a step to force it back into a matrix.)</div><div><br></div><div>When I get a chance, I’ll try to add a check into the function for such things.  We do not expect one would try to sort 24 values into 22 groups, so things like this elude us a bit.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers!</div><div>Mike</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
