><span><span> </span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;ID&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span><br></span></font><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Groups</span><span><span> </span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span>read</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span>table</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;Groups.txt&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><font><span><span> </span>h</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span>TRUE</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span><span> </span>sep</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;\\t&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span></font></div></code></div><div><br></div>When I subset using the columns Groups$Sp and Groups$Loc, it works perfectly. However, when I try subset using Groups$Ind, it returns an error:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div>&gt; land.sp &lt;- coords.subset(A=land, group=Groups$Sp) # By species</div><div>&gt; land.loc &lt;- coords.subset(A=land, group=Groups$Loc) # By locality</div><div>&gt; land.ind &lt;- coords.subset(A=land, group=Groups$Ind) # By individual</div><div>Error in dimnames(specimens) &lt;- `*vtmp*` : &#39;dimnames&#39; must be a list</div></div></code></div><br>I&#39;ve been using this approach successfully thus far, however this error occurred randomly from time to time. Now I just can&#39;ve tried changing the names of the factors, but it still didn&#39;t work. <br><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br>